Date: Mon, 16 Nov 2026 09:20:13 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/6] Use $XDG_DATA_HOME when $HOME is not set

Without $HOME there was no home directory at all, and so nowhere to write
the config and the savegames to, even when $XDG_DATA_HOME says where they
belong. That is the case on the PS4, where SDL sets the XDG base
directories up in the title's download data, and nothing sets $HOME.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.2 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01EVpxQnEDpmH9ifdSUZDpqm
---
 src/backends/unix/system.c | 11 +++++++++++
 1 file changed, 11 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/backends/unix/system.c b/src/backends/unix/system.c
index afb0e32f..cc26aa78 100644
--- a/src/backends/unix/system.c
+++ b/src/backends/unix/system.c
@@ -565,6 +565,17 @@ Sys_GetHomeDir()
 		const char* home = getenv("HOME");
 
 		if (!home) {
+#if defined(USE_XDG) && !defined(__HAIKU__)
+			// no home dir, but there may be an XDG
+			// dir: XDG_DATA_HOME/{cfgdir}
+			const char* xdgdatahome = getenv("XDG_DATA_HOME");
+
+			if (xdgdatahome) {
+				Com_sprintf(dir, MAX_OSPATH, "%s/%s/", xdgdatahome, cfgdir);
+				Sys_Mkdir(dir);
+				return dir;
+			}
+#endif
 			// uh-oh
 			return NULL;
 		}
